From 828f8702b2c9763c2d2f7a240a1297a37fa20635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sammydirksz@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:52:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: ipu-bridge: Add OVTI9734 (OV9734) to the supported
 sensors

The Microsoft Surface Laptop 2 has an OV9734 front camera (ACPI HID
OVTI9734, module MSHW0073) on IPU3 CSI-2 port 1. Without a table entry
the bridge creates no fwnode graph endpoint for it and the ov9734 driver
fails with -ENXIO in ov9734_check_hwcfg().

The ov9734 driver supports a single link frequency of 180 MHz on one
data lane, which matches the SSDB of this device (lanes = 1).

Tested on a Surface Laptop 2 (model 1769) with 7.3.4-surface:
ipu3-cio2 logs "Found supported sensor OVTI9734:00" and the sensor is
linked to ipu3-csi2 1.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Sam <sammydirksz@gmail.com>
Patchset: cameras
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
index 271b987660c5c72ebfa72b82697c2fa08469c56f..408da71c4075a64c8bd63066c3df574a0282bac4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -101,6 +101,8 @@ static const struct ipu_sensor_config ipu_supported_sensors[] = {
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI5675", 1, 450000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV8856 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI8856", 3, 180000000, 360000000, 720000000),
+	/* Omnivision OV9734 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI9734", 1, 180000000),
 	/* Sony IMX471 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("SONY471A", 1, 200000000),
 	/* Sony IMX471 (found on Lenovo X1 Carbon G14) */

